==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*andawlitiz}}, equivalent to {{m|ang|and||against, off}} + {{m|ang|wlītan||to look, behold}}. Cognate with Old Norse {{l|non|andlit}} (Swedish {{m|sv|anlete}}, Norwegian {{m|no|andlet}} and {{m|nn|andlit}}, Old High German {{m|goh|antlizzi}} (German {{m|de|Antlitz}}).

===Pronunciation===
